        "second_opinion": null,
        "why": "Both methods of FileHistoryManager load the per-file metadata from the cache with the same default and write it back. That is only a one-line shared ingredient, and a trivial _load_metadata helper would be marginal. The real operations differ. add_history appends a new entry, bumps the counter, and evicts the oldest entries beyond the max. pop_last_history removes the newest entry, reads and deletes its content, and handles a missing entry. They share no coherent reusable policy beyond cache get/set on the same schema, so this is not actionable duplication."
      },
